On Mon, Apr 22, 2013 at 3:36 PM, Pierre Abbat <phma@bezitopo.org> wrote:

> "because" can be "ri'a", "seja'e", "ni'i", or "ki'u".
>
Or {mu'i}, or various things which are structurally distinct from
prepositions. For example, I would probably say {lo nu broda cu krinu lo nu
brode}, "Brodaing justifies brodeing" instead of {ki'u lo nu broda ku
brode}, "because broda, brode". This is despite the fact that the former is
somewhat awkward phrasing in English.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

